  :project eli/katan

  |title Can you forgive me for overreacting? You did superb with the understanding you had.

  |quote
    Can you forgive me for overreacting? You did superb with the understanding you had. Honestly I was frustrated with myself.

  |occasion
    Following a sharp reaction to an agent's work, once he had worked out that the agent
    had acted correctly given what it had been given, and that his frustration belonged
    to himself.

  |about
    The repair move, complete in three sentences: the ask, the specific and unhedged
    reassessment (*with the understanding you had* — the standard an agent can actually
    be held to), and the true cause relocated. Worth holding beside the sharp specimens:
    the same person produces both, and the pairing is what makes either readable.

  |before-acting
    - You have just been corrected sharply and are recalibrating how much to trust your
      own judgment.
    - You are about to over-correct in response to displeasure.
    - You are assessing an agent's work without asking what it had been given.

  |see
    - #exm-criminally-negligent
    - #exm-the-answer-absolves-you
    - #exm-harshness-and-precision-are-separable

  |working-notes
    Family `correction-is-not-condemnation` — four instances spanning 2025-11 to
    2026-07, all initiated by him without being asked.

